Z||000000||ToddAsh||02-06-2001||04:12 PM||||I'd like to get some opinions on lowering.What are the disadvantages? I see from all the pictures that it looks great.Love my Fiero and this group is great.Got my car in November.Has only 15,162 miles.Added a spoiler,new stereo,keyless entry/alarm,and 16"wheels/tires.Want to lower,take off Cat,add rear sway bar.Just put on Classic tags.85's are eligible as of Jan.01.Thanks ,Todd Ash||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroLisa||02-07-2001||10:29 AM||||well since no one else appears to want to answer, i'll tell ya what I think  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> it looks good, but depending on where you live it may or may not be good. Since your in PA, I'm hoping you don't live anywhere in the mountains. I dated a guy out there, and the roads were hilly, pot-hole-y hell. wouldn't want a lowered fiero then. also if you're driving it in the winter, snow build-up isn't much fun.<BR>but it looks good!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Lisa<BR>86 gold 4 speed GT<BR>86 gold 5 speed SC (Sold!)<BR>Columbus, OH/Greensboro NC<BR>AOL IM: FieroLisa<BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/" TARGET=_blank>FieroLisa's Website</A><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierolisa/pffsig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Oreif||02-07-2001||10:42 AM||||Lowering a Fiero will stiffen the ride quality. How low and how stiff is up to you.<BR>The handling of the car increases greatly. The handling vs. ride quality is the big debate when lowering the car. As for how to lower it, lowering springs are the easiest, Lowered spindles are better (ride quality suffers less), Cutting the stock springs has been done but I personally wouldn't recommend it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Reality||02-07-2001||11:45 AM||||Would you want to look like a ricer????||||reg||5
Z||000004||Oreif||02-07-2001||12:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Reality:<BR><B>Would you want to look like a ricer????</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Lowering a Fiero isn't "ricer" it's when you lower it and stick on a set of 13" 40's and have the wheels stick out about 6".<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000005||1FST2M6||02-07-2001||12:33 PM||||the eibach pro-kit is abou1" lower just enought to notice the car is lowered but not enought to scrape on speed-bumps in the grocery store parking lot. Sustension Techniques and Jamex make sets but they are way lower.. Intrax alsomakes a set but agin.. in a pot hole laiden area i wouldn't recommend much more then 1" i drove my car through Michigan and i'll NEVER do that again.. mine is droped 2.5" on custom wound springs and i really should have had a kidney belt. <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst_side_1.jpg" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fst_side_1.jpg</A>   - lowered fine for my area.. NOT for snow or pot holes.. it acts great as a snow plow for my Grandmothers driveway when i was there... <P>got pics of your ride todd?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 02-07-2001).]||||reg||1
